# The product of balls with 2-limb centers, with the special states of a ball:
# ball_mul_2, then the fix-up of milestone1.md, "Ball kernels".
kernel:        ball_mul_2_full
input:         cx = cx0 cx1
input:         stored rx
input:         cy = cy0 cy1
input:         stored ry
output:        cw = cw0 cw1
output:        rw
value:         cx*cy
requires:      ball cx rx
requires:      ball cy ry
ensures:       encloses cw rw x*y x=cx,rx y=cy,ry
min_precision: 4
source:        ball_mul_2, then the fix-up of the special states of a ball (Milestone 1 listing)
license:       core: as ball_mul_2; fix-up: MIT
status:        proved
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   proved
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeBallCores.v ball_mul_2_full_correct
entry:         yes
ieee_only:     yes
cone_exempt:   the fix-up selects, after explicit tests that the center and the radius are finite (f) and that no operand is empty (e); B1 to B4 of milestone1.md, "Ball kernels", state what comes out

(cz0, cz1, rz) = ball_mul_2(cx0, cx1, rx, cy0, cy1, ry)
q              = add(rx, ry)
e              = eq(q, q)
a              = abs(cz0)
f1             = lt(a, const inf)
f2             = lt(rz, const inf)
f              = and(f1, f2)
c0             = select(f, cz0, 0)
c1             = select(f, cz1, 0)
r              = select(f, rz, const inf)
cw0            = select(e, c0, q)
cw1            = select(e, c1, q)
rw             = select(e, r, q)
